[00:49.94] One thing is sure I'd not be twenty-two
[00:56.71] As if that day when I first wandered there
[01:03.07] But mem'ries stay with me as mem'ries do
[01:09.51] 
[01:36.01] How fresh her mem'ry keeps for still I feel
[01:42.92] The velvet softness of her auburn hair
[01:49.54] And see again the moonbeams in her eyes
[01:55.74] As I did so long ago when I was there
[02:02.51] Youth called to youth in that now distant day
[02:09.15] I did not heed, my heart did not reveal,
[02:15.88] And now I know that love was born and lost
[02:22.33] In that little border town of Camooweal
[02:27.54] 
